do quickly retorts that there is if  you eat the sarlacc  it seems unlikely the great pit of  carcoon is the abandoned pit we see in  chapter 9.  the terrain is a lot different from the  scene featuring the beast in return of  the jedi  still the revelation that there is a  creature on tatooine capable of eating  sarlax gives us one possible explanation  for boba's survival  in the beginning of chapter nine's final  battle with the crate dragon mando  utters something that sounds like a  curse  as the beast begins to back up into his  lair mando says dank barrack it's going  back in  it's an expression that's repeated  throughout the rest of season 2 by mando  and other characters  while we don't know exactly what the  curse means it's a callback to the very  beginning of the mandalorian's first  episode  when we initially hear the phrase it's  spoken by mando's first bounty in the  series the blue skinned mithril mando  captures in a bar shortly after he and  his prisoner arrive at the razor crest  the fairy that brought them across the  ice is devoured by a monstrous rabbinic  and looks like mando's ship is its next  target as the pair quickly board the  craft the mithral yells out  dank barrick that was close it's  interesting that mando is now repeating  lines from a former bounty though he  doesn't quite find himself in the same  situation as the mithril  it always seems like mando can't take a  single step forward on his journey  without doing yet another job for  someone else first and chapter 10  is no different after his adventures in  and around most pell go mando returns to  mos  eisley to find another lead on  mandalorians and a task he has to  perform for the intel  the mechanic pelimoto introduces mando  to someone known only as the frog lady  who knows where a group of the elusive  warriors live  but she wants a trip back home in return  for the information as she's giving  mando the lowdown on what she knows  pelly translates for him she said her  hu