al outpost  as mando and his companions are on their  way out of the navarro imperial outpost  they come across a lab filled with  deformed bodies floating in tanks  in spite of their tight schedule the  heroes pause to access records to find  out what the lab is actually all about  mithril plays a hollow recording of dr  pershing the imperial doctor who works  on the child in the first season  among other things pershing reports  quote there were promising effects for  an entire fortnight  but then sadly the body rejected the  blood i highly doubt we'll find a donor  with a higher m count though  by higher em count dr pershing is  referring to one of the most  controversial pieces of the star wars  mythos midichlorians  in the phantom menace we learn that  every jedi's blood includes higher than  average amounts of midichlorians  and that is through communication with  these microscopic life forms that jedi  find their special connection to the  force  the fact that this concept still remains  so polarizing among some fans may be why  pershing says  m count rather than minichlorian count  allowing viewers on the thumbs down side  of the debate to imagine  m stands for something else at the same  time the presence of the lab and  pershing's recording have fed widespread  speculation that the experiments have  something to do with the cloning of  palpatine  and the creation of supreme leader snoke  chapter 13 of the mandalorian sees the  long-anticipated live-action premiere of  ahsoka tano played by rosario dawson  the former jedi teams up with mando  against the forces of magistrate morgan  ellsberg after some close calls ahsoka  defeats the magistrate in a duel  once she has else bit at her mercy  ahsoka demands to know one thing  now tell me where is your master  where is grand admiral thrawn thrawn is  a villain too good to be left on the  cutting room floor of star wars canon  the blue skin imperial first appeared in  timothy zahn's thrawn novel trilogy  starting with 1991's heir to the empire  and concluding with 1993's the last  command  while these novels have officially  joined the list of star wars media no  longer considered canon thrawn was also  featured in star wars rebels  ahsoka's lines let us know that thrawn  is still alive and it's extremely  important that she finds him  it could very well be that ahsoka's hunt  for the admiral will be the focus of the  upcoming disney plus ahsoka tano series  chapter 15 is another great example of  just how far mando is willing to go to  rescue grogu  with the aid of the newly appointed new  republic marshal kara dune  mando recruits former foe makes mayfield  to help him infiltrate an imperial  facility in order to access a computer  that can give him the location of mop  gideon  once they're inside mayfield refuses to  approach the computer console after  spotting a former commanding officer  mandel decides to do it himself and  makes a surprising choice to remove a  stormtrooper helmet he's wearing as a  disguise and expose his face  when mayfield's old commander starts  questioning mando he swoops in to save  the day  successfully bluffing the officer into  believing they're the genuine article  he also tries to make a quick work  excuse so they can get away from him  come on let's go fill out those tps  reports so we can go recharge the power  coil  mentioning tps reports is no doubt a  reference to the 1999 cult classic  office space in the comedy ron  livingston plays peter  a passionless office worker at a  software company who is being hounded by  supervisor bill lundberg about his tps  reports  um yeah you see we're putting the cover  sheets on  all tps reports now before they go out  though decades old now office base is  often still referenced and quoted by a  wide variety of fans  even in a galaxy far far away in chapter  15 mayfield reveals himself to be a much  more layered character than he  originally appears to be in the first  season  he and mando are corralled into sharing  drinks with the imperial officer valen  hess  the same officer mayfield avoids earlier  we soon learn hess holds an important  place in mayfield's history  one with such weight in fact that  mayfield allows it to overtake his  emotions and blow his cover  as hass asked for ideas for toast  mayfield suggests how about a toast  operation  cinder initially hess seems impressed by  mayfield turning to mando and saying now  there's a man who knows his history  we soon learned mayfield served under  hess during the operation and was  traumatized by what occurred  when you find out about operation cinder  his reaction is completely  understandable  it wasn't something dreamed up  specifically for the mandalorian but  instead has been mentioned in numerous  star wars video games comics and other  media  cinder is palpatine's contingency plan  in the case of his death to make sure  the galaxy's civilizations don't outlive  him  weeks after the battle of endor the  empire sets operation cinder in motion  using satellite arrays to cause  disastrous climate changes on different  planets including the boom  no official number has ever been given  for the amount of deaths but it was  clearly significant enough to make  mayfield shoot hess for his involvement  early in chapter 16 manda returns to  trask with allies  hoping to enlist the help of the  mandalorians he found there bogatan and  koska are not happy to see mando  accompanied by boba  whose voice they recognize is those of  the clones created on kamino  koska and boba exchange a few barbs  eventually leading to a brief  altercation  before things get violent bobo warns the  younger koska to calm down  she responds by saying you'll be talking  through the window of a back to tank  back to tanks aren't a particularly  obscure part of star wars lore though  you don't often hear them referred to by  name  there are cylindrical tanks filled with  bacta fluid which is known for its  healing properties  probably the most prominent use of a  bacta tank comes early in empire strikes  back when luke skywalker submerged in  one of the tanks after being rescued on  the planet hop by han solo  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  the mandalorian are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]  you

